  "architectural_notes": {
    "why_pkdgrav3_differs_at_256": "PKDGRAV3 (3.5.1, CUDA sm_86 FMM+Ewald) offloads P2P/M2L gravity tiles to GPUs while rebuilding the ORB/tree topology on host CPUs and performing full Domain Decomposition on steps where active rung <= 4 (67 DDs and 245 tree builds over 244 adaptive substeps). At 256^3 (16.78M particles), host DD (426s on 1G, 279s on 2G-MPI) + tree builds (522s on 1G, 146s on 2G-MPI) + host-device transfer overhead limit average GPU utilization to ~3-6% (~68W per A6000) and dominate wall time. By contrast, gravityCU holds all 16.78M particles GPU-resident end-to-end and skips full octree rebuilds on 279/312 active substeps via GPU lazy Hilbert refit (43-74% GPU utilization), delivering 29x faster wall time and 18-26x lower whole-node energy."
  }
